        "summary": "Microsoft co-founder, Bill Gates, has warned that reaching an international agreement on artificial intelligence could be more difficult than Cold War negotiations to limit nuclear weapons. His comments were made during an interview on NBC News’ “Meet the Press” and came as US President Donald Trump opposed calls for federal government safeguards on companies developing AI models. Gates argued that monitoring AI companies would not undermine the US in its competition with China's development of advanced technology. He also mentioned several international agreements with US leadership since World War II, including those concerning aviation safety, the ozone layer and nuclear weapons, and stated that the US and its allies had previously acted as “the fair actor” rather than exploiting their technological advantages.",
        "shortSummary": "Bill Gates warns that global agreement on AI will be more challenging than nuclear disarmament, advocating for stronger regulation and emphasizing the importance of collaborative efforts.",
