        "summary": "The list includes 11 shows that are family-friendly for teens and tweens. These include the classic Pritchard-Dunphey-Tucker sitcom, The Big Bang Theory, Malcolm in the Middle, and The Taskmaster. The British version of Tina Fey sitcom, All About All About The Stars, hosted by Jimmy Carr, features 10 well-known British comedians for six hours and features an offbeat sense of humour. The long-running medical sitcom, Malcolm In the Middle (Disney Plus and Apple TV), took a 16-year hiatus before returning to screens earlier this year. The show's original stars, including Frankie Muniz and Bryan Cranston, returned for a four-episode miniseries.",
